nodecode-birta is a rewrite of birtadev's birtadev/plugins:

  https://github.com/birtadev/plugins
  commit fd2485de51401db9dd9b25f0bc495bd36e9752c8
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 SP Krou Tech (LICENSE)

The original's hermes/ folder was a portable plugin manifest that named one
streamable-HTTP MCP server (mcp.json) and carried sixteen skills of
page-making guidance. The rewrite speaks that MCP protocol in Common Lisp --
initialize, notifications/initialized, tools/list, tools/call, with the
server's session id carried across requests -- and exposes the server's whole
tool surface through two Nodecode tools, birta_tools and birta_call, so a tool
the server adds needs no change here. The sixteen skills became one manual
topic, (help :birta), condensed.

Left out: the client-side OAuth sign-in step (Nodecode has no MCP browser
sign-in, so the section carries the token instead), the sixteen separate
skill files (one topic now), and the plugin manifest itself, which only a
plugin host reads.
